---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  TabsHero,
  TabsVariants,
  TabsMembers,
  TabsModels,
  TabsBuilder,
  TabsAgentPage,
  TabsSearchPopover,
} from "../../components/TabsDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Tabs"
  description="Switch between related panels of one page, panel, or setup flow."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Tabs</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A list of tabs that shows one panel at a time. Use it for sections of one
    page, views inside a panel, and the steps of a setup flow.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="tabs-demo"><TabsHero client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Tabs usage"
      code={`import {
  Tabs,
  TabsContent,
  TabsList,
  TabsTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/tabs";

<Tabs defaultValue="members">
  <TabsList aria-label="Members settings">
    <TabsTrigger value="members">Members (12)</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger value="invitations">Invitations</TabsTrigger>
  </TabsList>
  <TabsContent value="members">…</TabsContent>
  <TabsContent value="invitations">…</TabsContent>
</Tabs>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Tabs</code> holds the active value. Pass <code>defaultValue</code> to
      let it manage itself, or <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code> to
      control it from state or the address. Each <code>TabsTrigger</code> value matches
      one <code>TabsContent</code>. Give the list an <code>aria-label</code> that
      names the group.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants</h2>
    <p>
      <code>default</code> is a filled segmented control for a few settings groups.
      <code>line</code> underlines the active tab for page sections and views inside
      cards and popovers. <code>steps</code> fills the width for a numbered setup
      flow and uses the primary color, so the TulipFarm theme makes it green.
    </p>
    <TabsVariants client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Settings groups</h2>
    <p>
      The default list fits short labels and counts. <code>keepMounted</code> keeps
      both panels in the page, so a list keeps its place and its pending changes.
    </p>
    <TabsMembers client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Page sections</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Tabs from the address"
      code={`<Tabs
  value={tab}
  onValueChange={(value) =>
    navigate({ search: { tab: value === "access" ? undefined : value } })
  }
>
  <div className="max-w-full overflow-x-auto pb-1">
    <TabsList variant="line" aria-label="Model settings">…</TabsList>
  </div>
  <TabsContent value="access" keepMounted>…</TabsContent>
</Tabs>`}
    />
    <p>
      Wrap a long line list in a horizontal scroller so it never widens the
      page. The underline and focus ring stay inside the list. Panels can show
      loading, empty, and error states with <code>StatePanel</code>, or render
      nothing until their data is ready.
    </p>
    <div class="tabs-demo-group">
      <TabsModels client:load />
      <TabsAgentPage client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Setup steps</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Steps with markers"
      code={`<TabsList variant="steps" aria-label="Agent setup sections">
  {steps.map((step, index) => (
    <TabsTrigger key={step.id} value={step.id}>
      <span aria-hidden="true" className="grid size-5 place-items-center">
        {errors.has(step.id) ? <AlertCircle /> : done.has(step.id) ? <Check /> : index + 1}
      </span>
      {step.label}
      {errors.has(step.id) && <span className="sr-only">, needs attention</span>}
    </TabsTrigger>
  ))}
</TabsList>`}
    />
    <p>
      Put a number, a check, or a warning icon before each label, and add hidden
      text for the warning. Steps need room, so swap them for a select on small
      screens. The preview card uses a <code>line</code> list, and its Edit buttons
      move the setup to a step.
    </p>
    <TabsBuilder client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Inside a popover</h2>
    <p>
      Put a <code>line</code> list in a bordered header inside a <code
        >panel</code
      > popover. Leave out a trigger and its panel when an option does not apply,
      and fall back to another value. Without <code>keepMounted</code>, a panel
      unmounts when it is hidden.
    </p>
    <TabsSearchPopover client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="tabs-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      The four parts wrap Base UI Tabs. Every Base UI prop works, including <code
        >orientation</code
      >, <code>disabled</code> on a trigger, <code>activateOnFocus</code> and <code
        >loopFocus</code
      > on the list, <code>keepMounted</code> on a panel, <code>render</code>,
      and
      <code>className</code> as a string or a state function.
    </p>
    <p>
      Parts get <code>data-slot</code> values of <code>tabs</code>, <code
        >tabs-list</code
      >, <code>tabs-trigger</code>, and <code>tabs-content</code>. The list has <code
        >data-variant</code
      >, every part has <code>data-orientation</code>, and the active trigger
      has <code>data-active</code>. Mark trigger icons with <code
        >data-icon="inline-start"</code
      > or <code>"inline-end"</code> to tighten padding. <code
        >tabsListVariants()</code
      > returns list classes and <code>tabsListVariantNames</code> lists the variants.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The list is a <code>tablist</code>, each trigger is a <code>tab</code> with
      <code>aria-selected</code>, and each panel is a <code>tabpanel</code> labelled
      by its tab. Tab moves into the list and then to the panel. Arrow keys move between
      tabs and skip disabled ones, Home and End jump to the ends, and Enter or Space
      selects. Vertical lists use the up and down arrows.
    </p>
    <p>
      Colors and the underline change over 120–180ms. Both stop when reduced
      motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Tabs use <code>--sprout-secondary</code>, <code>--sprout-surface</code>,
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code
        >--sprout-line</code
      >, <code>--sprout-input</code>, <code>--sprout-primary</code>, <code
        >--sprout-focus</code
      >, <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>, <code
        >--sprout-shadow-control</code
      >, and the motion tokens. They follow light, dark, and the TulipFarm
      theme.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
